## 2. Frontend (`frontend/`)

**Stack:** Next.js 14 + TailwindCSS + TypeScript

### Key Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [page.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/frontend/src/app/page.tsx) | Home page with hero section and step cards |
| [VerifyForm.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/frontend/src/components/verify/VerifyForm.tsx) | Text input / URL input form that calls the backend API |
| [ResultsView.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/frontend/src/components/verify/ResultsView.tsx) | Displays verification results with claim cards |
| [api.ts](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/frontend/src/lib/api.ts) | API client ([verifyContent](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/extension/background.js#69-92), [verifyUrl](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/frontend/src/lib/api.ts#30-54), [healthCheck](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/frontend/src/lib/api.ts#68-80)) |
| [SourceReputationBadge.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/frontend/src/components/verify/SourceReputationBadge.tsx) | Shows domain reputation as a visual badge |
| [ConfidenceBreakdown.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/frontend/src/components/verify/ConfidenceBreakdown.tsx) | Visual breakdown of confidence scores |

### Flow
1. User pastes text or enters a URL in the `VerifyForm`
2. Frontend calls `POST /api/v1/verify/` (or `/api/v1/verify/url`)
3. Backend returns [VerificationResponse](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/backend/app/schemas/verification.py#196-231) with claims, verdicts, page score
4. `ResultsView` renders each claim with its verdict badge, confidence score, reasoning, and source links

---

## 3. Chrome Extension (`extension/`)

A **Manifest V3** Chrome extension that brings verification directly into the browser.

### Key Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [manifest.json](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/extension/manifest.json) | Extension config (permissions, context menus, keyboard shortcuts) |
| [background.js](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/extension/background.js) | Service worker: handles context menu clicks, messages, and API calls |
| [content/](file:///c:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/backend/app/api/v1/endpoints/verification.py#27-128) | Content script injected into web pages for text extraction and result highlighting |
| `popup/` | Extension popup UI |

### How it works
1. User right-clicks selected text → "Verify with Verique"
2. [background.js](file:///C:/Users/Saad/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/Verique/extension/background.js) sends the text to `POST /api/v1/verify`
3. Results are sent back to the content script which highlights claims inline on the page

---

## Data Flow Summary

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Frontend/Extension
    participant FastAPI
    participant VerificationService
    participant LangGraph Pipeline
    participant Groq LLM
    participant Web Search

    User->>Frontend/Extension: Paste text / select text
    Frontend/Extension->>FastAPI: POST /api/v1/verify/
    FastAPI->>FastAPI: Check cache
    FastAPI->>VerificationService: verify(text)
    VerificationService->>LangGraph Pipeline: run(text)
    LangGraph Pipeline->>LangGraph Pipeline: 1. Clean text
    LangGraph Pipeline->>Groq LLM: 2. Extract claims
    LangGraph Pipeline->>LangGraph Pipeline: 3. Filter claims
    LangGraph Pipeline->>Groq LLM: 4. Plan queries
    LangGraph Pipeline->>Web Search: 5. Fetch evidence
    LangGraph Pipeline->>LangGraph Pipeline: 6. Rank evidence
    LangGraph Pipeline->>Groq LLM: 7. Generate verdicts
    LangGraph Pipeline->>LangGraph Pipeline: 8. Format output
    LangGraph Pipeline-->>VerificationService: claims + verdicts
    VerificationService-->>FastAPI: page_score + summary
    FastAPI->>FastAPI: Cache result
    FastAPI-->>Frontend/Extension: VerificationResponse
    Frontend/Extension-->>User: Display results
```
